Comment: 
// @@@ If the starting index is greater than or equal to -1 and the result is not -1, then the bit at the result index is set to true.

We need to express: If (fromIndex >= -1) && (\result != -1) then this.get(\result) == true.

But also need to consider that method may throw exception if fromIndex < -1. The comment says "starting index is greater than or equal to -1". So premise: fromIndex >= -1. And result not -1. Then bit at result index is true.

Thus assert: assert (fromIndex >= -1 && \result != -1) => this.get(\result);

But need to be precise: this.get(\result) returns boolean. So we can write this.get(\result) == true or just this.get(\result). Usually assert expects boolean expression, so this.get(\result) is fine.

Thus final code:

<code>assert (fromIndex >= -1 && \result != -1) => this.get(\result);</code>

